---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';import PageIntro from '../components/PageIntro.astro';

import {site} from '../config/site';
---
<Layout title="Accessibility" description={`Care should feel open to you. Read the ${site.shortName} demonstration website’s accessibility.`}><PageIntro title="Care should feel open to you." eyebrow="Accessibility" items={[{name:'Accessibility'}]}/><section class="section container" style="padding-top:0"><div class="rich-copy"><h2>Our approach</h2><p>This site is designed with keyboard navigation, visible focus, descriptive labels, readable contrast and responsive layouts. We use semantic headings and native controls where possible.</p><h2>Motion & visual alternatives</h2><p>The site respects your device’s reduced-motion setting. Animated 3D scenes switch to static artwork, and scroll effects are disabled. Treatment comparisons support keyboard-controlled range inputs and include explanatory captions.</p><h2>Forms & navigation</h2><p>Forms identify required details and show validation messages near their fields. The mobile menu supports keyboard focus and Escape to close. A skip link moves directly to the main content.</p><h2>Help with a barrier</h2><p>If a page or control is difficult to use, contact the team through the contact page and describe the page, device and issue. Do not include medical information. A live practice should also offer an accessible phone or alternative booking channel.</p><h2>Ongoing review</h2><p>Accessibility requires continuing testing with assistive technologies and real users. This statement describes the project’s design intent and testing, not a certification of universal compatibility. Reviewed September 24, 2026.</p><p style="margin-top:2rem"><a href="/contact">Contact the team ↗</a></p></div></section></Layout>
